n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $5\\text{th}$ Fourier sine coefficient of $4f(x)-g(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417678 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "236925ac-8f18-52a6-be78-880a69837dd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417678 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $4f(x)-g(x)$ are\n\n- $4{a}_{0}-{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $4{a}_{n}-{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $4{b}_{n}-{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $5$th sine coefficient of $4f(x)-g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n4{b}_{5}-{d}_{5}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417682 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417682 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417682 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417682 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the constant Fourier coefficient of  $3f(x)+6g(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417682 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86928bbe-ce4d-5454-a36f-1b092e7b6f03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417682 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $3f(x)+6g(x)$ are\n\n- $3{a}_{0}+6{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $3{a}_{n}+6{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $3{b}_{n}+6{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the constant Fourier coefficient of $3f(x)+6g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n3{a}_{0}+6{c}_{0}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510759 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510759 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510759 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510759 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510759 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510759 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510759 #edb/ref 1045 "Properties of Fourier Series" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510759 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186511644 #edb/ref 17592186045